    "segments": [
      {
        "start": 0.0,
        "end": 5.41,
        "text": "This is what cinnamon does to the sugar in your body."
      },
      {
        "start": 5.41,
        "end": 8.69,
        "text": "In a glass of warm water, mix one teaspoon of cinnamon,"
      },
      {
        "start": 8.69,
        "end": 10.49,
        "text": "a squeeze of fresh lemon juice,"
      },
      {
        "start": 10.49,
        "end": 12.45,
        "text": "and one tablespoon of raw honey."
      },
      {
        "start": 12.45,
        "end": 14.53,
        "text": "Now, if you wanna take this to the next level,"
      },
      {
        "start": 14.53,
        "end": 17.43,
        "text": "add a slice of fresh ginger to get your digestion moving,"
      },
      {
        "start": 17.43,
        "end": 19.73,
        "text": "a pinch of turmeric to calm the inflammation,"
      },
      {
        "start": 19.73,
        "end": 21.73,
        "text": "and a tiny pinch of pink salt"
      },
      {
        "start": 21.73,
        "end": 24.49,
        "text": "so your body holds onto water instead of bloat."
      },
      {
        "start": 24.49,
        "end": 26.97,
        "text": "Mix it well, then drink this on an empty stomach"
      },
      {
        "start": 26.97,
        "end": 28.05,
        "text": "every single morning."
      },
      {
        "start": 28.05,
        "end": 30.69,
        "text": "By day three, your energy starts coming back."
      },
      {
        "start": 30.73,
        "end": 33.05,
        "text": "Day five, your clothes start fitting better."
      },
      {
        "start": 33.05,
        "end": 34.29,
        "text": "And after only a week,"
      },
      {
        "start": 34.29,
        "end": 36.77,
        "text": "you'll finally start feeling like yourself again."
      },
      {
        "start": 36.77,
        "end": 38.95,
        "text": "But let's be honest, grating ginger"
      },
      {
        "start": 38.95,
        "end": 42.09,
        "text": "and measuring six ingredients every morning is annoying"
      },
      {
        "start": 42.09,
        "end": 43.45,
        "text": "and nobody sticks with that."
      },
      {
        "start": 43.45,
        "end": 46.09,
        "text": "That's why I just add one scoop of Jupy Hydration,"
      },
      {
        "start": 46.09,
        "end": 47.97,
        "text": "all important ingredients in one scoop."
      },
      {
        "start": 47.97,
        "end": 49.57,
        "text": "It goes right into my morning water"
      },
      {
        "start": 49.57,
        "end": 51.21,
        "text": "and tastes like fresh blood orange."
      },
      {
        "start": 51.21,
        "end": 52.97,
        "text": "If you're dealing with bloating every day,"
      },
      {
        "start": 52.97,
        "end": 55.85,
        "text": "you can find it by searching Jupy Hydration on Amazon"
      },
      {
        "start": 55.85,
        "end": 57.39,
        "text": "or just check the link in my bio."
      },
      {
        "start": 57.39,
        "end": 58.75,
        "text": "And if you're watching on Facebook,"
      },
      {
        "start": 58.75,
        "end": 60.25,
        "text": "the link is in the description."
      }
    ],
    "text": "This is what cinnamon does to the sugar in your body. In a glass of warm water, mix one teaspoon of cinnamon, a squeeze of fresh lemon juice, and one tablespoon of raw honey. Now, if you wanna take this to the next level, add a slice of fresh ginger to get your digestion moving, a pinch of turmeric to calm the inflammation, and a tiny pinch of pink salt so your body holds onto water instead of bloat. Mix it well, then drink this on an empty stomach every single morning. By day three, your energy starts coming back. Day five, your clothes start fitting better. And after only a week, you'll finally start feeling like yourself again. But let's be honest, grating ginger and measuring six ingredients every morning is annoying and nobody sticks with that. That's why I just add one scoop of Jupy Hydration, all important ingredients in one scoop. It goes right into my morning water and tastes like fresh blood orange. If you're dealing with bloating every day, you can find it by searching Jupy Hydration on Amazon or just check the link in my bio. And if you're watching on Facebook, the link is in the description."
  },
